WEB→NATIVE PARITY MAP (SOCRouteChart.tsx is the spec; every branch + label reproduced)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ChartContainer title "Battery Along Route"   → SOCRouteChartHeader  [i18n tripPlanner.socChart.title]
  ariaLabel "Planned route battery state-…"    → Chart .accessibilityLabel
                                                 [i18n tripPlanner.socChart.aria]
                                                 + .accessibilityValue = points/start/arrival/min/stops summary
  chartData = socCurve.map round(distance_m*10)/10, round(soc*10)/10
                                                → SOCRouteChartProjection.samples (rounded1)
  <AreaChart> green→amber→red url(#socGradient) → AreaMark LinearGradient stops
                                                 success(.40)/warning(.20)/danger(.10) top→bottom
  <Area stroke="#22c55e">                       → LineMark Color.TS.statusSuccess, 2pt
  <YAxis domain={[0,100]} label "SOC %">        → .chartYScale(0...100) ticks 0/25/50/75/100,
                                                 .chartYAxisLabel [i18n tripPlanner.socChart.col.soc]
  <XAxis dataKey="distance" label "km">         → continuous x = sample.distance,
                                                 .chartXAxisLabel "km" [i18n tripPlanner.socChart.axis.distance]
  <ReferenceLine y={minArrivalSOC} "Min n%">    → horizontal RuleMark danger dashed [6,4]
                                                 + SOCRouteChartMinArrivalLabel "Min n%" [i18n .min]
  stopDistances walk (|soc-charge_from_soc|<5,  → SOCRouteChartProjection.chargeMarkers
   cumulative advance, round(distance_m))         (verbatim port; tolerance 5; ordinal = matched index+1)
  <ReferenceLine x={dist} "⚡ Stop i+1">         → vertical RuleMark speed(#3b82f6) dashed [4,4]
                                                 + SOCRouteChartStopLabel bolt + "Stop n" [i18n .stop]
  <Tooltip> "{v} km" / "{v}% SOC"               → .chartXSelection → nearest sample → SOCRouteChartTooltip
  chartData.length === 0 ? <EmptyState> : <area>→ SOCRouteChartProjection.hasTrace (≥1) → .content/.empty
  EmptyState "Plan a trip to see the SOC curve" → ContentUnavailableView [i18n tripPlanner.socChart.empty]
  <FadeIn> (ChartContainer)                     → TSFadeIn
  (P4 widening) web content/empty → full native envelope: + loading skeleton, + error/retry
                (QueryError parity), + stale/offline freshness chip & banner (ADR-013).

